{"packet_id":"D007-01","doc_id":"D007","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"California security deposit cap (AB 12)","requirement":"Landlords may generally charge at most one month's rent as a security deposit (last month's rent counts, first month's rent does not); certain small landlords may charge up to two months, and deposits must be returned within 21 days.","key_value":"1 month's rent; up to 2 months' rent for certain small landlords","coverage_conditions":"All residential rentals; smaller cap exceptions for landlords owning only two rental properties with no more than four residential units total held by a natural person, family trust, or LLC of natural persons.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"landlord owning only two rental properties with no more than four residential units total","unit_limit":4}],"per_tenancy":"Photograph-before-tenancy duty applies to tenancies beginning on or after July 1, 2025.","coverage_quotes":["Starting July 1, 2024, landlords who own only two rental properties with no more than four residential units total can charge up to two months' rent for furnished and unfurnished units if ownership is held by a natural person, family trust, or limited liability company (LLC) where all members are natural persons"]},"exemptions":"Landlords owning only two rental properties with no more than four residential units total, held by a natural person, family trust, or LLC whose members are all natural persons, may charge up to two months' rent.","penalty":null,"effective_date":"2024-07-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"AB 12","quoted_span":"Starting July 1, 2024, many landlords may only charge one month's rent for unfurnished and furnished units","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D007-01","doc_id":"D007","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Berkeley Rent Ordinance security deposit interest","requirement":"For units fully or partially covered by Berkeley's Rent Ordinance, landlords must pay tenants interest on their security deposit at the end of each year, and a prorated amount if the tenant moves out before the end of the year.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Units fully or partially covered by Berkeley's Rent Ordinance.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":["For tenancies in units fully or partially covered by Berkeley's Rent Ordinance, landlords must pay tenants interest on their security deposit at the end of each year and a prorated amount if the tenant moves out before the end of the year."]},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"Berkeley Mun. Code ch. 13.76","quoted_span":"For tenancies in units fully or partially covered by Berkeley's Rent Ordinance, landlords must pay tenants interest on their security deposit at the end of each year and a prorated amount if the tenant moves out before the end of the year.","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D007-01","n_rules":2,"note":null}

